      "kind": "abbreviation",
      "question": "How does solids retention time affect ammonium left in the effluent?",
      "answer": "[1] Solids retention time (SRT) affects the amount of ammonium (NH4+-N) left in the effluent by influencing the establishment and stability of nitrifier population. As SRT increases from 5 days to approximately 15 days, the removal of NH4+-N concentration falls steeply, reaching low residual values by the 12-15 days range. This indicates that longer SRT leads to a more stable and established nitrifier population, which helps in reducing NH4+-N in the effluent. Beyond 15 days, the removal of NH4+-N shows diminishing returns.",
